{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"agentty.agentty","latestVersion":"0.9.50","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) agentty contributors","description":"Blazing-fast Claude in your terminal — a C++26 alternative to claude-code.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/1ay1/agentty/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) agentty contributors","description":"Blazing-fast Claude in your terminal — a C++26 alternative to claude-code.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/1ay1/agentty/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"agentty is a native C++26 terminal coding agent and a drop-in alternative to claude-code. A single static binary with sub-millisecond cold start, sandboxed by default, and one-command SSH air-gap. No Node, Python, or Electron. Signs in with your Claude Pro/Max subscription or an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.","moniker":"agentty","name":"agentty","packageUrl":"https://agentty.org/","publisher":"agentty","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/1ay1/agentty/issues","publisherUrl":"https://agentty.org/","releaseNotes":"Changed\n- Tool cards got a full visual pass. The header is one two-tone pill:\n  the tool name on a solid chip, the rest on a soft band of the same\n  colour, and the output below sits on a faint tint of it. Write, edit and\n  diff output is syntax coloured on the red/green bands, and paired lines\n  light up the words that changed. Grep rows are syntax coloured too, and\n  every match sits on an amber band. File paths get a language dot and a\n  dim directory with a bold file name, and edit headers end with +3 −5.\n- Grep highlights whatever the pattern matched, regex included. It used\n  to give up on any pattern with an escape like resolve\\(.\n- Running tools keep their spinner whenever the whole card fits on\n  screen, instead of a still dot, and their header has a soft shimmer.\n- Permission prompts show what bash will run. bash was missing from the\n  shell case, so approving it showed the whole args object as json.\n- Every theme reads. A contrast floor lifts colours that were too dim on\n  their own background (links, headings, hints), keeping the hue. Across\n  the 615 bundled themes that took 870 dim colours to none.\n- The native theme gets the same look on terminals that report their\n  colours: maya asks once at startup, in the round-trip it already makes.\n- Reasoning uses a quiet neutral ink instead of the theme's secondary hue,\n  says how many lines are hidden when collapsed, and its rail is coloured\n  again (a renderer bug left left-only borders uncoloured).\n- Smaller: failed cards drop repeated [kind] tags, the composer colours\n  @file and /command, nested markdown lists indent, picker rows and the\n  diff review panel use the same tinted bands, MCP tools read as\n  Search Issues · github, and the ── branch before each tool is gone.\nAdded\n- tool_gallery renders every surface from real recorded tool calls\n  (--running, --ask, --chrome, --reasoning, --prose, --welcome,\n  --panels), and a ui_snapshots test diffs its output so a change that\n  alters how something looks shows up in review.\nFull history: CHANGELOG.md","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/agentty-org/agentty/releases/tag/v0.9.50","tags":["ai","claude","cli","coding-agent","developer-tools","terminal"]}},"longDescription":"agentty is a native C++26 terminal coding agent and a drop-in alternative to claude-code. A single static binary with sub-millisecond cold start, sandboxed by default, and one-command SSH air-gap. No Node, Python, or Electron. Signs in with your Claude Pro/Max subscription or an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.","moniker":"agentty","name":"agentty","packageUrl":"https://agentty.org/","publisher":"agentty","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/1ay1/agentty/issues","publisherUrl":"https://agentty.org/","releaseNotes":"Changed\n- Tool cards got a full visual pass. The header is one two-tone pill:\n  the tool name on a solid chip, the rest on a soft band of the same\n  colour, and the output below sits on a faint tint of it. Write, edit and\n  diff output is syntax coloured on the red/green bands, and paired lines\n  light up the words that changed. Grep rows are syntax coloured too, and\n  every match sits on an amber band. File paths get a language dot and a\n  dim directory with a bold file name, and edit headers end with +3 −5.\n- Grep highlights whatever the pattern matched, regex included. It used\n  to give up on any pattern with an escape like resolve\\(.\n- Running tools keep their spinner whenever the whole card fits on\n  screen, instead of a still dot, and their header has a soft shimmer.\n- Permission prompts show what bash will run. bash was missing from the\n  shell case, so approving it showed the whole args object as json.\n- Every theme reads. A contrast floor lifts colours that were too dim on\n  their own background (links, headings, hints), keeping the hue. Across\n  the 615 bundled themes that took 870 dim colours to none.\n- The native theme gets the same look on terminals that report their\n  colours: maya asks once at startup, in the round-trip it already makes.\n- Reasoning uses a quiet neutral ink instead of the theme's secondary hue,\n  says how many lines are hidden when collapsed, and its rail is coloured\n  again (a renderer bug left left-only borders uncoloured).\n- Smaller: failed cards drop repeated [kind] tags, the composer colours\n  @file and /command, nested markdown lists indent, picker rows and the\n  diff review panel use the same tinted bands, MCP tools read as\n  Search Issues · github, and the ── branch before each tool is gone.\nAdded\n- tool_gallery renders every surface from real recorded tool calls\n  (--running, --ask, --chrome, --reasoning, --prose, --welcome,\n  --panels), and a ui_snapshots test diffs its output so a change that\n  alters how something looks shows up in review.\nFull history: CHANGELOG.md","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/agentty-org/agentty/releases/tag/v0.9.50","tags":["ai","claude","cli","coding-agent","developer-tools","terminal"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.50/app.json","detailSha256":"a69269e4aa8c86222a5033e8b924ce59de0d7b5e5438e121783d023c54ef2667","releaseDate":"2026-11-07","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"0.9.50"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.49/app.json","detailSha256":"93603e0d40d81987da0a1f17395d922efd61bfde0d36c25ba046cd1b4c9ddbbd","releaseDate":"2026-11-06","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"0.9.49"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.48/app.json","detailSha256":"7feeb337caaf723702b097d9bc0b855d8cb5bb303d06a6f0c02368c6f450a5ce","releaseDate":"2026-11-06","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"0.9.48"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.47/app.json","detailSha256":"70dd5c57c7953e0000df1b7c94204d0db8d5cd87ae888f13ba4711807c79faf3","releaseDate":"2026-11-06","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"0.9.47"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.46/app.json","detailSha256":"937ea84595dc1644713f104bd78af614e8fd0aee560c3bc31d125f739dd1c3de","releaseDate":"2026-11-05","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"0.9.46"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.45/app.json","detailSha256":"bd33e0b8447a36089de7d241cf6fcf182f9067edc72a4a2f3a47fb2fc1e0b668","releaseDate":"2026-11-03","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.9.45"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.44/app.json","detailSha256":"5def4992276355ef4516f00dcda324276cca3b622ae8bd85393ea8eca87ba4ec","releaseDate":"2026-11-03","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.9.44"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.43/app.json","detailSha256":"e2f6bf9cc3a72b25d360e611954d371e58d0628964090adc2c87fe1e438dbd2c","releaseDate":"2026-11-03","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.9.43"},{"architect